  "correctAnswer": "A",
  "explanation": "Since the graph has an $x$-intercept at $(6,0)$, substituting these coordinates into the function gives $0 = a(6-3)^2 + 12$. This simplifies to $0 = a(3)^2 + 12$, or $0 = 9a + 12$. Solving for $a$ gives $9a = -12$, so $a = -\\frac{12}{9} = -\\frac{4}{3}$.\n\nWhy B is incorrect:\n\nThis results from incorrectly inverting the fraction, computing $a = -\\frac{9}{12}$ instead of $-\\frac{12}{9}$.",
